IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ca-jarrah`

-- Corporations Act 2001 (Cth), ss 9AC, 46, 50, 113, 117, 180-184, 191, 201A, 201B, 254A, 254T, 257A-257D, 606, 674, 674A, 676, 708, 1042A, 1043A, 1272B, 1272C -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_corporations-act-2001.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Facts from Daniel's life (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-daniel): Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd registered on
-- 15 March 2031, Daniel 34, 70% his, 10% Priya's, 20% a sophisticated investor's for $500,000, with a director identification
-- number (d043); Series A on 1 September 2035, $5,000,000 for 25% from a fund that is a sophisticated investor (d050); a
-- selective buy-back of the investor's shares on 31 March 2042 (d064); Jarrah acquires Formly on 15 June 2043 (d065); Jarrah sold
-- to a listed buyer for $40,000,000 on 30 June 2050 (d071); a non-executive directorship of a listed company from 1 September
-- 2051 (d073); angel investments in five start-ups on 20 March 2056 (d081).
-- ENCODER'S ASSUMPTIONS, not in the scenario: Daniel is Jarrah's sole director; the voting split after the Series A (Daniel 525,
-- Priya 75, the investor 150, the fund 250 of 1,000 votes) assumes no other issue; Jarrah has fewer than 50 members in 2050;
-- the fund's gross assets; Daniel's gross assets after the sale; every certificate date and every vote. The s 708(8)(c) net assets
-- and gross income amounts ($2,500,000 and $250,000 below) are HYPOTHETICAL inputs: the Act leaves them to regulations.

